        "content": "<p>fitzgen requested <a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/bytecodealliance/teams/wasmtime-compiler-reviewers\">wasmtime-compiler-reviewers</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15224\">PR #15224</a>.</p>",
        "id": 639264173,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794341383
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"thumbs up\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"thumbs up\">:thumbs_up:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15224#pullrequestreview-5849713074\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 639284189,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794346314
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15224#discussion_r4530751206\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Perhaps a builder-style setter for <code>may_throw</code> rather than an alternative constructor?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 639284192,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794346314
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15224#discussion_r4530788283\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>FWIW I believe we could put quite a few functions into this set. For example all lowered component functions have this property because you can't ever throw an exception across component boundaries anyway. This could probably also be true for pretty much all our own libcalls, too. Perhaps a good follow-up issue?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 639284193,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794346314
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15224#discussion_r4530758234\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This feels a bit confusing to me where whatever <code>self.may_throw</code> was prior it's unconditionally overwritten here. Could this perhaps be conditional, as well was be accompanied by a comment for why this is needed and what it's doing?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 639284195,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794346314
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15224#pullrequestreview-5849781963\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 639284466,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794346396
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15224#discussion_r4530802328\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Question on this: this looks like it's doing half of a <code>call $imported_function</code> manually and then letting <code>Call.indirect_call_inst(..)</code> do the rest - would it be possible to make this look like a full-on call since there's a <code>callee_index</code> anyway?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 639284468,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794346397
    },
